import GQ2.Dyadic.Instances.MpcC6WeightedRelationSupport

/-!
# Checked final class-six weighted trace

This module closes the 65-factor depth-five endpoint.  An external generator selected 65
relation rows, but no external equality is trusted: every row is an explicit `Deriv`, its
Boolean check is reduced by the kernel, and `Deriv.sound` supplies its group equality.  The
only global assembly is semantic permutation of commuting depth-five factors followed by
kernel-proved cancellation of duplicate pairs.  Ten rows use the guarded top-layer Jacobi
rule; all remaining rows expand exact restricted-square consequences using existing group
rules and depth deletion.

The resulting public path proves the reflected endpoint, the original concrete class-six
certificate equality, and `MpcMkFullSupply 4 mpcFvW5`.  There is no opaque finite-certificate
axiom and no trusted output from the generator.
-/

namespace GQ2.Dyadic.Instances.MpcC6WeightedTraceFinal

